[Slack Thread](https://stackexchange.slack.com/archives/CBVG8MJQN/p1752065324499899)

Someone is trying to to SQLi us: https://opserver.main-prod.int.gcp.stackoverflow.net/exceptions?q=requested+value&store=

That's futile, but the noise in the exception log is annoying, and the fact that they're getting an error page probably makes them think they're onto something 🙄

## To Test

1. Try first on main
2. Go to a random question page.  This error shows up when `POST`ing to ShowQuestion (weird, right?).  This is normally fired when changing the sort order.  To try with malicious values, run the following in your dev tools console...

    ```js
    var resp = await fetch(location.pathname + '?sortOrderPreference=hi', { 
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
            "X-SO-fkey": StackExchange.options.user.fkey
        }
    })
    var text = await resp.text()
    
    console.log(text)
    ```

3. You should see an error show up in [`/errors`](https://meta.stackexchange.local/errors)

    ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bf33120e-cfb1-406d-a59c-6b49c2657f26)

4. You can also try a happy one just confirm the script should work

    ```js
    var resp = await fetch(location.pathname + '?sortOrderPreference=CreatedDesc', { 
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
            "X-SO-fkey": StackExchange.options.user.fkey
        }
    })
    var text = await resp.text()
    
    console.log(text)
    ```

6. Pull down the PR and do the same thing. The error should no longer show up
7. Confirm changing tab preference still works and persists across page loads

## Summary

*Setting target to esnext*

This became an issue attempting to use `$state()` within a class. 
An example of the class, `question-model.svelte.ts` which is a valid Svelte 5 class.

```
export class QuestionModel implements QuestionData {
    title: string = $state();
    body: string = $state();
    tags: string[] = $state();

    constructor(props: Partial<QuestionData>) {
        this.title = props.title ?? "";
        this.body = props.body ?? "";
        this.tags = props.tags ?? [];
    }

    clear(): void {
        this.title = "";
        this.body = "";
        this.tags.length = 0;
    }
}
```

The following error was being returned:
```
Error: CompileError: state_invalid_placement: `$state(...)` can only be used as a variable declaration initializer or a class field
https://svelte.dev/e/state_invalid_placement
_Scripts/islands/ask-question/src/question-model.svelte.ts:4:21
2:     constructor(props) {
3:         var _a, _b, _c, _d, _e, _f, _g, _h, _j, _k;
4:         this.title = $state();
                                ^
5:         this.body = $state();
6:         this.tags = $state();
```

This requires the use of at least `es2022`. Was told that we could just use `esnext` to stay current.

This PR introduces the generation of TypeScript classes for client side product events.
It aims to remove the risk that there is a mismatch in event properties when emitting events from the client side.

It will take a C# `ClientOriginatedStackEvent` like this:

```csharp
/// <summary>
/// The popover is shown to the user.
/// </summary>
[ProductEvent("stacklive.helper-cta.seen")]
public record HelperCtaSeen : ClientOriginatedStackEvent
{
    public string SessionId { get; set; }
    public string Origin { get; set; }
    public string RequestSessionId { get; init; }
    public string MatchingMechanism { get; init; }
    public string[] TagsMatched { get; init; }
}
```

and generates this:

```typescript
export class HelperCtaSeen {
    public static readonly EventName: string = "stacklive.helper-cta.seen";

    constructor(
        public readonly matchingMechanism: string,
        public readonly origin: string,
        public readonly requestSessionId: string,
        public readonly sessionId: string,
        public readonly tagsMatched: string[]
    ) {
        this.matchingMechanism = matchingMechanism;
        this.origin = origin;
        this.requestSessionId = requestSessionId;
        this.sessionId = sessionId;
        this.tagsMatched = tagsMatched;
    }
}
```

