## Summary

This PR adds the ability for fragment proxies to forward `Set-Cookie` headers from upstream services to the client. This is controlled via a new configuration setting, `shouldForwardCookies`. 

By default, this setting is `false`, preserving existing behavior. It has been explicitly enabled for the `ai-assist` fragment to allow that service to manage state via cookies.

## How to Test
*I tried to get this deployed to main-test to test in a live environment, but the `deploy-to-google-cloud-ascn-dev` label does not seem to work.

To test locally:
- Update your local AskStack code to set a cookie.  
e.g.
```cs
app.Use(async (context, next) =>
{
    context.Response.Cookies.Append("MY-TEST", "DoesItWork");
    await next();
});
```
- Navigate to [https://meta.stackexchange.local/ai-assist](https://meta.stackexchange.local/ai-assist) and verify the cookie is forwarded through.
